// Tool-neutral MCP server catalog.
//
// Add your real MCP servers here, one entry per server, keyed by server
// name. Setup steps for each tool (Claude Code, Codex CLI, pi) read this file
// and render it into that tool's native MCP config format/container.
//
// Keep commands portable: use `$HOME` and `$REPO` placeholders instead of
// absolute paths so this file works across machines and checkouts. Setup expands
// both tokens from its verified repository and home inputs before registration.
// Runtime `${ENV_VAR}` interpolation is preserved for the native client.
//
// SECURITY: this file is PUBLIC (deny-list + secret scanner gate pushes).
// Only put shareable servers here -- use $HOME/$REPO placeholders and
// `${ENV_VAR}` interpolation for tokens; never inline secrets or internal
// hostnames. Personal servers belong in each client's native user configuration,
// never in this public catalog. Native Pi uses ~/.pi/agent/mcp.json.
//
// Native Pi disablement uses `enabled: false`. The `disabled` compatibility
// field serves other catalog consumers; the Pi renderer removes it.
{
  "example-server": {
    "command": "npx",
    "args": ["-y", "@scope/mcp-server"],
    "env": {},
    "enabled": false,
    "disabled": true
  }
}
